I'm not sure how I managed to put this typo in there, but the variable 'means' in the dmbern() distribution for z should be 'mean'. With the typo, I got the same error you did. With that fixed, I get the same error I mentioned in the first post. That said, your point that I 'don't necessarily need to worry about the reported error message' is well taken. In fact, everything seems just fine. I am able to simulate the data z, and after doing so model$calculate() works without the error.

For what it's worth, I am at least using nimble 0.8.0, even if I can't read NIMBLE output very well.

Many thanks for taking a look!

Henry

